 "summary": "Mostly no. MACD line above or below its signal line did no better than random entries on 1h, 4h or daily, and crosses on 4h and daily stayed inside the luck band too. One narrow result holds up: on 1h in downtrends, price kept falling after a cross down, 0.09% more than after random candles, at 10 and 20 candles and without its strongest stretch.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Going long on a bullish cross (MACD crosses up signal)",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "On 1h, entries after a cross up were 0.1% ahead of random after 20 candles, but at that horizon only. On 4h and daily they stayed inside the luck band."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting a bearish cross (MACD crosses down signal)",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "On 1h the pooled result came from SOL and showed at 20 candles only. In downtrends it held at 10 and 20 candles. In uptrends, and on 4h and daily, it showed nothing."
  },
  {
   "use": "Trend filter (MACD line above or below signal)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Inside the luck band on 1h, 4h and daily, long or short, pooled and in both trend regimes."
  },
  {
   "use": "Faster signal line (MACD(12,26,5) crosses up)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Inside the luck band on 1h, 4h and daily. Its one fragile result, daily in downtrends, disappears without the signals between Dec 26, 2022 and Jan 2, 2023."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, going long after the MACD line crossed up through its signal line gave 6,152 entries in 3,605 separate moves. After 20 candles they were 0.1% ahead of random entries, just above a luck band that topped out at 0.07%. At 10, 50 and 100 candles the gap was chance. In uptrends it was 0.13% ahead with the same one-horizon shape. In downtrends it showed nothing.",
  "Shorting after a cross down on 1h beat random entries by 0.08% after 20 candles, pooled. BTC and ETH sat inside the luck band at 0.01% and 0.02%, and SOL carried the result at 0.22%. Split by regime, the short held in downtrends: 0.09% better than random, at 10 and 20 candles, and still there without the signals on Nov 7–8, 2022, during the FTX collapse. In uptrends it showed nothing.",
  "On daily, the pooled crosses look like chance in both directions, but the regimes pull apart. Long entries on a cross up did 4.05% worse than random in uptrends and 4.02% better in downtrends. Both are fragile. The uptrend loss disappears without four signals between Dec 2, 2021 and Jan 15, 2022, and the downtrend gain shows at 20 days only. The short on a cross down was 3.5% worse than random in downtrends, and that rests on one signal on Dec 28, 2022.",
  "MACD line above its signal line, used as a level condition, enters on far more 1h candles than the cross up, because it holds for long stretches. It finished 0.01% behind random entries, inside the band in both regimes. MACD line below its signal line for shorts did the same. The faster signal line, MACD(12,26,5), gives about 1.3 times as many crosses up on 1h as the default and lands inside the band on 1h, 4h and daily.",
  "For a long DCA bot, a MACD cross adds nothing you can count on. The 1h gain shows at 20 candles and is gone by 50, so your take profit and DCA orders decide the result. The shape worth testing is a 1h short bot that pairs the cross down with a filter for price below the 200-day SMA, with a take profit sized for a move that plays out within 10 to 20 candles. That breaks in uptrends, where the same cross showed nothing. On daily, leave MACD crosses out of the start condition: the results flip sign between regimes and depend on a handful of signals."
 ],
